WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:09.540
﻿Hyper mega launcher incoming!

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.940
﻿Block it!

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.010
﻿Go!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.120
﻿We did it!

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.470
﻿- Darn it.
- ﻿One more shot!

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.300
﻿- Rifle, maximum power!
﻿- Okay!

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.990
﻿The Build Strike.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:00.490
﻿It's a customized Gunpla
﻿based on the Strike Gundam.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.530
﻿Its main weapon is
﻿a medium-type beam rifle.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.500
﻿Presumably, the output of
﻿the beam is variable.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.440
﻿And at high output, it rivals
﻿that of a hyper mega launcher.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.610
﻿Such a high output...
﻿How does the rifle endure it?

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.740
﻿Please look at this.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:23.780
﻿The barrel interior probably uses
﻿metal parts for improved durability.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.850
﻿Also, the shield withstood
﻿a shot from a hyper mega launcher.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.920
﻿Considering its
﻿state of damage afterwards,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.300
﻿it may be a normal shield overlaid
﻿with thin, narrow plastic boards.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.900
﻿That would take such perseverance...

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:45.370
﻿Did that boy build it all by himself?

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.070
﻿It's fate.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:51.210
﻿The builder, Sei Iori, is the son of

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.410
﻿the runner-up in the 2nd Gunpla Battle
﻿Championship World Tournament.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.820
﻿Remember Takeshi Iori?

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.690
﻿I see. No wonder.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.730
﻿Even so, our victory is unshakeable.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:10.130
﻿A battle has already begun...

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.800
﻿Before you enter the battlefield.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.620
﻿Kirara!

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:36.720
﻿Thank you, everybody!

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.920
﻿Kiraran!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.910
﻿You've made it through round two.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.120
﻿For now, congratulations, Reiji.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.590
﻿It was easy.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:24.490
﻿With Sei's Gunpla and me,
﻿we can beat any—

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:25.590
﻿Not so fast.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.930
﻿What?

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:31.870
﻿Gunpla has a long history that
﻿you still know nothing about.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:37.140
﻿If you lower your guard,
﻿somebody will trip you up.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.280
﻿Are you're saying that's you?

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.010
﻿Keep on winning, Reiji.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.780
﻿I look forward to seeing you
﻿at the World Tournament.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.420
﻿World Tournament...

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.290
﻿It seems that I've got
﻿yet another reason not to lose.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.160
﻿Right, Sei?

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.970
﻿Sei.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.210
﻿What is it, mom?

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.110
﻿Would you find the Gunpla that
﻿the customer is looking for?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.950
﻿I don't know much about them.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:24.950
﻿Thank you.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.090
﻿Ah, excuse me.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.330
﻿What kind of Gunpla
﻿are you looking for?

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:36.300
﻿I'm looking for a GM kit.
﻿The Cold Districts Type from 0080.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.230
﻿Oh, that. It's over here.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.440
﻿Is this the one?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.670
Yes, this is it. Thank you!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.110
﻿No problem.
﻿Are you familiar with Gunpla?

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.280
﻿I love the GMs from "War in the Pocket".

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:56.750
﻿The GM Command,
GM Command Space Type, GM Sniper II...

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.960
﻿The Draken-E included with
﻿the GM Sniper II was cute, too.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.820
﻿That's the Riah forces'
﻿middle mobile suit, right?

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.230
﻿Yeah, that's it!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:18.110
﻿You have questions about
﻿the Gunpla you bought the other day?

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.940
﻿Would you like to build it here?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.660
﻿You're the one I met in
﻿the place called "school".

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.860
﻿Did you come to see Sei?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.940
﻿Who's that girl?

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.710
﻿Hey, didn't you come to see Sei?

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:54.940
﻿What's with her?

00:06:58.550 --> 00:06:59.710
﻿Hey, Sei.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:00.910
﻿What?

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.850
﻿That chick in the store,
﻿is she your girlfriend?

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:07.790
﻿No, it's not like that.
﻿She's just a customer.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:10.790
﻿You seemed to be
﻿hitting it off with her.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:13.090
﻿We were talking about Gundam.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.130
﻿Alright. How boring.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.170
﻿﻿I've never met a girl who
knows so much about Gundam.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:25.370
﻿You're participating in
﻿the Gunpla Battle Championship?

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.610
﻿For now. I'm past round two, but...

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.580
﻿Wow, amazing.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.010
﻿Oh stop.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.750
﻿When's the third round?
﻿I'll go cheer for you.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.320
﻿There's no need.
﻿It would be embarrassing if I lost.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.860
﻿I can tell from looking at your display.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.860
﻿There's no doubt
﻿that your Gunpla are strong.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.430
﻿You think?

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:03.210
﻿Good morning, Kousaka.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.510
﻿Morning.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.880
﻿Did you build the Gunpla
﻿you bought the other day?

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.390
﻿If you have any questions, please ask me.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.490
﻿What is it?

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.560
Uh...

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.630
﻿It's nothing.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.060
﻿Okay.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:33.110
﻿The girl I was talking with
﻿at the store yesterday?

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.840
﻿She was just a customer.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:37.880
﻿We were just talking about Gunpla.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.180
﻿Why do you ask?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.540
﻿Ah, Iori.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:07.240
﻿What's wrong, Kousaka?

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.980
﻿You dropped your bag.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.050
﻿That girl...

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:16.850
﻿Do you know her?

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:20.350
﻿I think I've seen her before
﻿at a Gunpla Battle venue.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:24.020
﻿I could be mistaken, though.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.800
﻿Miss Mihoshi, why did you
﻿come to see me?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.570
﻿Do I need a reason to come see you?

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.200
﻿No, it's not like that.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:40.510
﻿But how did you know
﻿I went to the Seiho Academy?

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.350
﻿Oh, that was feminine intuition.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.500
﻿You're like a Newtype.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.950
Oh, yes. Would you like some tea?

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.820
Thank you. I'll have some.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.530
﻿And...

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:07.170
﻿I wonder if I could see the Gunpla
﻿you made for the championship.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.570
﻿Sure, I have it with me right now.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.540
﻿Here.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.840
﻿It's as cool as I expected!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.440
﻿- Can I touch it?
- ﻿Sure.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.350
﻿Wow. It's based on the Strike.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.120
﻿You really know it well.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:27.220
﻿Impressive. Its rifle and shield
﻿are completely original...

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:29.590
﻿It must've taken you days.

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:31.190
﻿Yeah, sort of.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:34.160
﻿Is this backpack transformable?

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.800
﻿Yes. And don't tell anyone, but...

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.230
﻿There's a gimmick to this backpack.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.640
﻿Really? What is it?

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.180
Well...

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.680
﻿Excuse me.
﻿I need to use the bathroom.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.750
﻿Yeah, I'll wait here.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.480
﻿Okay.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:11.260
﻿Excuse me.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.840
﻿That's Iori's Gunpla...

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.440
﻿Yeah, I asked him to show it to me.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.580
﻿Who are you, anyway?

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.110
﻿Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.680
﻿Kousaka?

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.550
﻿Why are you here?

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.790
﻿I'm sorry ﻿if I gave you the wrong idea.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.980
﻿Sei was just showing me his Gunpla.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:40.990
﻿So don't worry.
﻿Sei was just showing me his Gunpla.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.240
﻿So don't worry.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.400
﻿Thank you, Sei.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.170
﻿I'll see you at the store again.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.870
﻿Oh, yes. Thank you.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:54.210
﻿Kousaka?

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.250
﻿I see.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.520
﻿So this is youth.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.900
﻿Are you leaving, miss?

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.140
﻿That weird old guy.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:29.510
﻿﻿You must be here because
you're interested in Gunpla Battle.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:30.340
﻿Let's go.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:31.880
﻿Um...

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:35.050
﻿Where we're going,
﻿you'll see ultimate battles.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:36.580
﻿Besides, you can get in for free.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.390
﻿It's not that...

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:02.380
﻿In the third round of the
﻿regional qualifying tournament,

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.010
﻿the winner of match one
﻿is Tatsuya Yuuki.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.910
﻿His Zaku's been tuned up even more.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.950
﻿He's something.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.490
﻿His Gunpla was already so perfect.

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:18.360
﻿Ours is still stronger.
﻿We'll prove it in this tournament!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.630
﻿I'm looking forward to it.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:26.000
﻿But before that, you should
﻿concentrate on round three.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:30.570
﻿Your next opponent has won
﻿the first two rounds by default.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:32.240
﻿You should watch out.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.710
﻿- By default?
﻿- You've got a problem with—

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.040
﻿We shall now begin match seven.

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:40.010
﻿It's our turn. Let's go, Sei!

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:40.960
Oh, yeah.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:50.860
﻿Their battle is just about to begin.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.130
﻿Iori.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.500
﻿One, two...

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:59.100
﻿Kirara!

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:27.590
﻿Hi. I'm your idol, Kirara!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.230
﻿Kiraran.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:32.030
﻿Kiraran!

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:35.140
﻿- What the heck is that?
- ﻿Don't ask me.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.200
﻿That girl...

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.010
﻿Kirara!

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:39.570
﻿A fan?

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:44.510
﻿So she is...

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.820
﻿Be careful, Iori.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.520
﻿Hello, I'm Kirara.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.520
﻿Don't be too hard on me.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:55.720
﻿Let's finish this swiftly.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.460
﻿Don't get distracted, okay?

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:03.530
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:12.170
<i>﻿Field 5, City.</i>

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.040
<i>﻿Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:21.850
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.090
﻿- Build Strike Gundam.
- ﻿Let's go!

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:30.590
﻿Kirara, here I go!

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.430
﻿The Gerbera Tetra!

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:39.370
﻿It was originally going to be
﻿the prototype Gundam Unit 4.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.170
﻿- You're a smart guy.
- ﻿So what!?

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:51.510
﻿So fast!

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.950
﻿Big deal!

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.320
- ﻿What!?
﻿- Why?

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.240
﻿What's going on, Sei!?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.470
﻿How is this possible...?

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:25.910
﻿The joint parts are scratched.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.050
﻿How'd that happen?

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.890
﻿I haven't allowed anyone to
﻿touch the Build Strike.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:36.460
﻿No... It can't be...

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.790
﻿Yes, you're right. Kiraran.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.730
﻿Are you Miss Mihoshi!?

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.300
﻿As I thought...

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.230
﻿Miss Mihoshi...

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.900
﻿She came to me knowing that
﻿I was her next opponent?

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:54.070
﻿And she scratched my Gunpla
﻿on purpose.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:59.550
﻿A battle begins before
﻿you enter the battlefield.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.450
﻿Go, Gerbera Tetra!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:11.960
﻿Darn you!

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:15.930
﻿Miss Mihoshi, are you happy
﻿winning battles like this?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.270
﻿It only dishonors your Gunpla
to win in such a way!

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:22.640
<i>﻿You're sweet, Sei.</i>

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.440
<i>﻿But I'm not interested
﻿in Gundam or Gunpla.</i>

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:30.510
﻿My agency decided to promote me
﻿as an Akihabara-style Gunpla idol.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.510
﻿So I studied intensively.

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:37.020
﻿I watched over 20 anime series
﻿that I don't understand well.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:39.990
﻿I memorized names
﻿like Zaku and Gouf.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.560
﻿And I mastered plastic model
﻿construction and techniques.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:49.060
﻿Sometimes, I wondered
﻿if I was an idol or a modeler.

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:54.300
﻿But I kept working hard...

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.000
﻿To make my dream come true!

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.140
﻿Yes, to become a top idol!

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:06.550
﻿That's not true. If you didn't
﻿really like Gunpla,

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:09.680
﻿you couldn't have built
﻿such a strong Gerbera Tetra!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:12.650
<i>﻿Who said I built it myself?</i>

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:13.490
﻿Huh?

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:19.630
<i>﻿I had my fans build it
﻿in exchange for two-shot photos.</i>

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.960
﻿I'll do anything it takes
﻿to win this battle.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.100
﻿If I win, I'll get media exposure.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.270
﻿The more they cover me,
﻿the more famous I'll become.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.740
﻿I'll be able to debut as a singer,
﻿and release my first album.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.610
There's a shining stage...

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:39.780
﻿Waiting for me in the big arena!

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.150
﻿The shield!

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:44.620
﻿I'm sorry, Sei.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:47.290
﻿I'll make it up by
﻿sending you arena tickets!

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:52.930
﻿- Oh no!
﻿- Iori!

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:54.490
Sei!

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.500
﻿Reiji, the twelfth slot.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.040
﻿What!?

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:10.840
﻿The backpack transformed!

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.780
﻿It's a fighter... no, a booster?

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.450
﻿What the heck is that?

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.690
﻿There's a gimmick to this backpack.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:24.590
﻿That's what he was talking about!?

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.860
﻿Your name's Kirara, right?

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.500
﻿I don't hate people who
﻿challenge the impossible.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.440
﻿I like daring people like you.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:39.740
﻿But...

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:43.540
﻿We also have reasons
﻿why we can't lose!

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:57.060
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:00.890
﻿No way. My dream...

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:03.760
﻿Kirara's dream...

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:17.410
﻿Sei, don't let it get you down.

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:21.380
﻿I'm afraid I can't chat with her
﻿about Gundam anymore.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:25.250
﻿What?
﻿I thought you had a thing for her.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:29.620
﻿No way. I told you that
﻿she's just a customer.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:33.860
﻿If I teach her the joys of Gunpla,

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:36.030
﻿I bet she'll come to love it!

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.970
﻿All that effort for nothing...

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.730
﻿Let's try again together!

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:44.040
﻿I'll build you a stronger Gunpla!

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.540
﻿I can't wait another year!

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.180
﻿Fat chance.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:54.410
﻿Congratulations, Sei and Reiji.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.250
﻿Thank you, Mr. Ral.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:57.880
﻿It was rough going, though.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:03.390
﻿A warrior grows by facing hardship
﻿and overcoming it.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.330
﻿Iori.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:11.530
﻿Kousaka, you came to cheer for me?

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:13.970
﻿Congratulations, Iori and Reiji.

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:16.270
- ﻿Thanks.
﻿- Thank you, Kousaka.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:19.940
﻿And...

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:21.710
﻿What is it?

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:26.050
﻿I'm not sure how to build
﻿the Gunpla I bought from you.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.050
﻿Will you teach me some time?

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.420
﻿Of course.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.090
﻿You wanna come to my store right now?

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.990
﻿Yeah, let's go.

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:26.130
﻿Well done, Iori.

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:29.070
﻿You've easily surpassed
﻿what I anticipated.

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:30.540
﻿I can't afford to slack off.

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:31.940
﻿Tatsuya.

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:35.980
﻿Allan! Why are you here?

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:38.810
﻿Tatsuya, listen to me soberly.

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:40.850
﻿The master fell sick.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:43.720
﻿The master!?

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:45.850
﻿That's why I'm here.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.620
﻿To pick you up.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:52.530
﻿And to make you
﻿give up the name of Yuuki.

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:59.260
﻿Just looking at it, I understand
﻿that his Gunpla is something else.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:01.630
Next episode, "The Strongest Builder".

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:05.020
You still don't know the true Gunpla Battle.
